<!--
    SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-or-later
    SPDX-FileCopyrightText: 2026 BorderKeys contributors

    The two builds are separate packages and can be installed at the same time, so all four
    names a user is shown have to tell them apart: the launcher, the settings activity, the
    input-method picker, and the entry in every application's text-selection menu. Leaving any
    of them alone gives a list with two identical entries and no way to know which is which
    without opening one — and the selection menu is the worst place for that, since both
    entries would sit side by side with nothing else on screen to tell them apart by.

    The library modules own the last two, and an application's resources win over a library's,
    which is why they are overridden here rather than in a flavour of each module.
-->
<resources>
    <string name="app_name" translatable="false">BorderKeys +</string>
    <string name="settings_activity_label" translatable="false">BorderKeys +</string>
    <string name="ime_name" translatable="false">BorderKeys +</string>
    <string name="process_text_label" translatable="false">Draft with BorderKeys +</string>
</resources>
